          "The relational gospel agrees that these are true realities and that the Spirit makes them our own. Where it differs is over <em>scope</em> (were they true of humanity before faith? see the next question) and <em>method</em>. It treats the list as a love letter to receive, not a performance checklist. A “position” that never touches the heart is not what Paul had in mind: he prays that Christ may “dwell in your hearts through faith” (Eph 3:17)."
